    "theorem": "BinarySemaevIrreducibilityAudit.actual_binary_S3_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem actual_binary_S3_certificate : (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [CharP K 2] (b : K), Irreducible (ordinaryMv b) ∧ (ordinaryMv b).IsSymmetric ∧ (∀ x y z : K, MvPolynomial.eval ![x,y,z] (ordinaryMv b)=BinaryS3Audit.binaryS3 b x y z) ∧ ∀ (L : Type) [Field L] (f : K →+* L), Irreducible (MvPolynomial.map f (ordinaryMv b))) ∧ (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [CharP K 2] [IsAlgClosed K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K), W.Δ≠0 → W.a₁=1 → W.a₃=0 → W.a₄=0 → ∀ x y z : K, MvPolynomial.eval ![x,y,z] (ordinaryMv W.a₆)=0 ↔ ∃ P Q R : W.Point, SemaevS3.pointX P=some x ∧ SemaevS3.pointX Q=some y ∧ SemaevS3.pointX R=some z ∧ P+Q+R=0) ∧ sourceMv (0:ZMod 2) 0=binaryFactor^2 ∧ ¬ IsUnit binaryFactor ∧ ¬ Irreducible (sourceMv (0:ZMod 2) 0) ∧ ordinaryMv (0:ZMod 2)≠sourceMv (0:ZMod 2) 0",
    "decl_sha256": "79d3d696a33624dfc64c9584dc199c88467791f72304ccdb252c318667770424",
    "scope": "Actual ordinary characteristic2 S3=(xy+xz+yz)^2+xyz+b is symmetric and absolutelyirreducible after every field scalar map, allb. Evaluation matches existing BinaryS3 and actual Mathlib point zero-sums on every nonsingular a1=1,a3=a4=0 ordinary model over algclosedfield, all repeatedcoordinates/two-torsion included. Actual Artin-Schreier change and rationalfunction degree1pole obstruction; primitive/injective algebraicclosure coefficient embedding/Gauss and MV equiv proved, not premises. Explicit shortF2a=b0nonunit square/directnotirreducible and polynomialinequality distinguish models. No square-root, finite-enumeration, nonsingularity or irreducibility premise for algebraic theorem; actual group bridge retainsnonsingularity. No qualifiedsource refutation/novelty/nativeexperiment. Generalhigherarity absoluteirred and splitsk>=3open.",
